/* book Worked example 2: Q: The same air (1 kg, 300 K, 100 kPa) is compressed to one-eighth of its volume along pV1.3 = C. Find p₂, T₂, W, ΔU and Q.
   1. p₂ = 100 × 81.3 = 100 × 14.929 = 1493 kPa.
   2. T₂ = 300 × 80.3 = 300 × 1.8661 = 559.8 K.
   3. W = mR(T₁ − T₂)/(n − 1) = 0.287 × (300 − 559.8)/0.3 = 0.287 × (−259.8)/0.3 = −248.6 kJ.
   4. ΔU = mcv(T₂ − T₁) = 0.718 × 259.8 = 186.6 kJ.
   5. Q = ΔU + W = 186.6 − 248.6 = −62.0 kJ.
   6. Check with cn = 0.718 × (1.3 − 1.4)/0.3 = −0.2393 kJ/kg·K: Q = −0.2393 × 259.8 = −62.2 kJ, the same within rounding (the data 0.718 and 1.4 are each rounded).
   Answer: p₂ = 1493 kPa, T₂ = 559.8 K, W = −248.6 kJ, ΔU = +186.6 kJ, Q = −62.0 kJ: the gas gets hotter and still rejects heat. */
